\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"4e54221cb5aa\",{\"children\":[\"Health\"]}]]}]]}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"flex flec-col md:flex-row items-center justify-center xl:justify-between p-2 \",\"style\":{\"flexBasis\":\"33%\",\"backgroundColor\":\"$undefined\"},\"data-component\":\"dynamic_layout_block\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-5 py-8 items-center\",\"data-component\":\"stack\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L19\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"rounded\",\"src\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4ij0poqn/production/bac6f4ec02ebb1bf2e547d5646be677e29310165-500x400.png?fit=max\u0026auto=format\",\"alt\":\"Labrador retriever breed fact rate card\",\"width\":500,\"height\":400,\"children\":\"$undefined\"}]]}]]}]]}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"2\",{\"data-component\":\"container__with_modules\",\"className\":\"p-2\",\"style\":{},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"data-component\":\"container__default\",\"className\":\"container mx-auto px-6 md:px-4 \",\"style\":{},\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col md:flex-row\",\"data-component\":\"dynamic_layout\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex flec-col md:flex-row items-center justify-center xl:justify-between p-2 \",\"style\":{\"flexBasis\":\"66%\",\"backgroundColor\":\"$undefined\"},\"data-component\":\"dynamic_layout_block\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-5 py-8 items-center\",\"data-component\":\"stack\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"data-component\":\"container__default\",\"className\":\"container mx-auto px-6 md:px-4 \",\"style\":{},\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-left\",\"data-component\":\"textblock\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"035a63f09cbf\",{\"id\":\"about-the-labrador-retriever-breed\",\"className\":\"my-5 font-neucha text-3xl\",\"children\":[\"About the Labrador retriever breed\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"f5020122adf6\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"Labrador Retrievers originate from the Newfoundland region of Canada, where they were initially bred by fishermen to retrieve ducks and other game from water. Their journey to becoming one of the world's most beloved breeds began when they were taken back to England and further developed into the loyal and versatile dogs we know today.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"47369f1e20be\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"Labradors are not only popular family pets but also excel as working dogs, thriving in roles such as guide dogs, gun dogs, and even search and rescue. They are renowned for their happy and intelligent nature, exceptional sense of smell, and a love of food, which makes them highly trainable.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"4926d87eae54\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"This breed has captured hearts worldwide, appearing as iconic fictional characters like Marley from \\\"Marley and Me\\\" and the Andrex puppy. Labradors have also achieved real-world fame, such as Endal, the most decorated dog in history, who earned numerous awards for his gallantry and service, including the PDSA's Gold Medal for Animal Gallantry.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"6ce0c2d2f190\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"Labradors are also central to BorrowMyDoggy’s story, as the inspiration for the platform came from Aston, a chocolate Labrador borrowed by our founder, Rikke.\"]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",\"169cade1c14f\",{\"id\":\"weight-height-life-expectancy\",\"className\":\"my-5 font-neucha text-2xl\",\"children\":[\"Weight, height \u0026 life expectancy\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"467f93e3ba78\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"Physically, Labradors range in height from 54 to 57 cm and weigh between 25 and 36 kg, with working/American types being lighter and more agile compared to the stockier show/English types. Their lifespan typically spans 11 to 13 years, but some, like Adjutant, the oldest Labrador on record, have lived to the remarkable age of 27 years and 3 months!\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"6939127cfa30\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"With their versatility, loving nature, and rich history, Labrador Retrievers continue to be one of the most cherished and admired breeds around the world.\"]}]]}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"flex flec-col md:flex-row items-center justify-center xl:justify-between p-2 \",\"style\":{\"flexBasis\":\"33%\",\"backgroundColor\":\"$undefined\"},\"data-component\":\"dynamic_layout_block\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-5 py-8 items-center\",\"data-component\":\"stack\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L19\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"rounded\",\"src\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4ij0poqn/production/8d82e3a0f88110753a80bcf2ea0889172593c69d-3768x3768.jpg?fit=max\u0026auto=format\",\"alt\":\"One black and one yellow Labrador retriever sitting on the grass\",\"width\":500,\"height\":500,\"children\":\"$undefined\"}]]}]]}]]}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"3\",{\"data-component\":\"container__with_modules\",\"className\":\"p-2\",\"style\":{\"backgroundColor\":\"#dce6f5\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-5 py-8 items-center\",\"data-component\":\"stack\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"data-component\":\"container__default\",\"className\":\"container mx-auto px-6 md:px-4 \",\"style\":{},\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-left\",\"data-component\":\"textblock\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"249426b8d001\",{\"id\":\"what-is-the-temperament-of-labradors-like\",\"className\":\"my-5 font-neucha text-3xl\",\"children\":[\"What is the temperament of Labradors like?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"5eaaa9fb46ec\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"Labradors are renowned for their friendly, intelligent, and good-natured temperament, making them one of the most popular and beloved dog breeds worldwide. Their loyal and affectionate nature ensures they form strong bonds with their families, thriving as both family pets and working dogs.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"c1a74a8aab27\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"Labradors are generally patient and gentle, making them an excellent choice for households with children. They have a reputation for adoring children and their famously kind and loving disposition. Their social nature also extends to other animals, as they typically get along well with other pets when properly introduced.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"a80b79b7d20a\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"Playful and full of energy, Labradors excel in activities that allow them to retrieve and explore, such as fetching games. Their love for water is undeniable, so they’ll enthusiastically enjoy a swim—just ensure they stay in safe areas and don’t venture too far.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"7c7df7467d84\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"Labradors’ combination of intelligence and eagerness to please makes them highly trainable and adaptable to various lifestyles. Whether they’re playing with children, swimming, or simply lounging with their family, Labradors bring a sense of joy, companionship, and warmth to every moment.\"]}]]}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"4\",{\"data-component\":\"container__with_modules\",\"className\":\"p-2\",\"style\":{},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-5 py-8 items-center\",\"data-component\":\"stack\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"data-component\":\"container__default\",\"className\":\"container mx-auto px-6 md:px-4 \",\"style\":{},\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-left\",\"data-component\":\"textblock\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"eef13b66cfb2\",{\"id\":\"our-labrador-retriever-community\",\"className\":\"my-5 font-neucha text-3xl\",\"children\":[\"Our Labrador retriever community\"]}]]}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"data-component\":\"container__default\",\"className\":\"container mx-auto px-6 md:px-4 \",\"style\":{},\"children\":[\"$\",\"