nt\":\"stack\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"data-component\":\"container__default\",\"className\":\"container mx-auto px-6 md:px-4 \",\"style\":{},\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-left\",\"data-component\":\"textblock\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"294e32d1524f\",{\"id\":\"what-kind-of-exercise-do-labradors-need\",\"className\":\"my-5 font-neucha text-3xl\",\"children\":[\"What kind of exercise do Labradors need?\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"0c6e5bc406d1\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"Labradors are an energetic and active breed that thrives on regular physical and mental stimulation. A healthy adult Labrador typically requires around 2 hours of exercise daily, although this can vary depending on their individual needs, age, and fitness level. Their exercise routine should include a mix of walking, running, swimming, and opportunities to engage their senses through sniffing and investigating their surroundings.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"0f0d52629654\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"Exercise for Puppies:\",[\"$\",\"br\",\"node-1\",{}],\"While Labrador puppies are full of energy, their exercise needs are different to avoid overexertion and protect their developing joints. A general guideline is 5 minutes of exercise per month of age, split across multiple short sessions throughout the day. Puppies should not transition to full adult exercise levels until they are at least 18 months old and fully grown.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"c5a290cac0eb\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"613d8b3093ee0\",{\"children\":[\"Activities Labradors Enjoy:\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",\"2cfd5c00fee4-parent\",{\"className\":\"list-inside list-disc\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"2cfd5c00fee4\",{\"className\":\"ml-4\",\"children\":[\"Retrieving Games: Labradors excel at retrieving, making activities like fetch or flyball ideal. These not only provide physical exercise but also engage their natural instincts.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"6b14cb456292\",{\"className\":\"ml-4\",\"children\":[\"Swimming: Labradors are natural water lovers. If you have access to a safe, controlled area, swimming is a great low-impact activity they’ll adore. Throwing a floatable toy for them to retrieve adds extra fun.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"3187a96e96c9\",{\"className\":\"ml-4\",\"children\":[\"Mental Stimulation: Incorporate activities that engage their brains, such as treat-hiding games or puzzle toys. These help combat boredom and reduce the likelihood of undesirable behaviours.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"8d411acda541\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"5fcf26da10720\",{\"children\":[\"Importance of Balance:\"]}],\"\",[\"$\",\"br\",\"node-2\",{}],\"Without adequate exercise and stimulation, Labradors can become bored, which may lead to mischief or destructive behaviours. Regular mental and physical activities keep them well-behaved, easier to train, and content in their daily lives.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"82171d8ed7bf\",{\"className\":\"w-full mb-5\",\"children\":[\"By tailoring their exercise to their age and providing a variety of activities, you can ensure your Labrador stays fit, happy, and healthy.\"]}],[\"$\",\"h3\",\"20d057b1515a\",{\"id\":\"\",\"className\":\"my-5 font-neucha text-2xl\",\"children\":[\"\"]}]]}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"flex flec-col md:flex-row items-center justify-center xl:justify-between p-2 \",\"style\":{\"flexBasis\":\"33%\",\"backgroundColor\":\"$undefined\"},\"data-component\":\"dynamic_layout_block\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-5 py-8 items-center\",\"data-component\":\"stack\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L19\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"rounded\",\"src\":\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4ij0poqn/production/e571d8b6270ca8175a9a84f105ba2e8aa37ca36b-3024x3024.jpg?fit=max\u0026auto=format\",\"alt\":\"Fox red Labrador on the beach\",\"width\":500,\"height\":500,\"children\":\"$undefined\"}]]}]]}]]}]}],[\"$\",